---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { withBase } from "../lib/url";
import meet from "../../config/meet.json";
import site from "../../config/site.json";

const { lastYearSent, lastYearLabel, estimatedEligible } = site.headlineStats;
const unusedSpots = meet.rosterCap - lastYearSent;
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Home"
  description="Arizona could send 80 swimmers to the Western Zone Age Group Championships. Last year it sent 14. Find out in ten seconds whether your swimmer already qualifies."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="hero-kicker">Western Zone Age Group Championships</p>
    <h1 class="hero-headline">
      Arizona can send <strong>{meet.rosterCap}</strong> swimmers.<br />
      In {lastYearLabel}, it sent <strong>{lastYearSent}</strong>.
    </h1>
    <p class="hero-sub">
      Around <strong>{estimatedEligible}</strong> Arizona swimmers had already swum a qualifying time
      that year. Most of them never found out. <strong>{unusedSpots} spots went unused.</strong>
    </p>
    <a class="button-primary button-lg" href={withBase("/calculator")}>
      Check if your swimmer qualifies →
    </a>
    <p class="hero-note">Takes about ten seconds. No sign-up, nothing saved, nothing sent anywhere.</p>
  </section>

  <div class="card callout">
    <h2 class="card-heading">Wait — what is Zones?</h2>
    <p>
      It's the biggest meet most 14-and-under swimmers in the West can reach. Every LSC in the
      Western Zone sends a team each summer, and swimmers race for <strong>Arizona</strong> rather
      than for their club — team caps, team warmups, the whole thing.
    </p>
    <p style="margin-bottom:0">
      To be eligible, a swimmer needs to be 14 or under on the meet's first day and to have swum
      <strong>one AAA time</strong>. That's it. One time, in any one event, in any course.
      <a href={withBase("/faq")}>More about what the week is like →</a>
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="card">
    <h2 class="card-heading">Why do so many kids miss it?</h2>
    <p>
      Mostly because nobody tells them. There's no letter home when a swimmer hits a qualifying time
      — a kid can swim a AAA cut in March and nobody mentions it until the deadline has passed.
    </p>
    <p style="margin-bottom:0">
      If you think your swimmer might be close, the fastest thing you can do is
      <strong>check the time yourself</strong>, then ask your coach:
    </p>
    <ul class="tight-list ask-list">
      <li>Is my swimmer eligible for Zones?</li>
      <li>How does Arizona pick the team?</li>
      <li>When is the entry deadline?</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="note" style="margin-bottom:0">
      Your coach is your best resource here — they know the process, the deadlines, and your
      swimmer. This site just helps you know what to ask.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="tile-grid">
    <a class="tile" href={withBase("/my-times")}>
      <span class="tile-title">Track my swimmer</span>
      <span class="tile-desc">Log best times, watch the gap to AAA close. Stays on your device.</span>
    </a>
    <a class="tile" href={withBase("/standards")}>
      <span class="tile-title">AAA Standards</span>
      <span class="tile-desc">Every cut, every event, all three courses.</span>
    </a>
    <a class="tile" href={withBase("/faq")}>
      <span class="tile-title">Cost &amp; Travel</span>
      <span class="tile-desc">What the week looks like, and what it costs.</span>
    </a>
  </div>

  <p class="note" style="margin-top:1.5rem">
    🚧 Still being built: the eligible-swimmer board and the "What It Took" benchmarks. The
    calculator, tracker and standards all work today.
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
